<title>ITALY: Table of Italy's main three-year economic targets.</title>
<headline>Table of Italy's main three-year economic targets.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the main percentage targets contained in the three-year economic forecasts document approved by Italy's cabinet on Friday.  </p>
<p>						     1998	1999	2000</p>
<p>Deficit-GDP ratio without budget cuts    4.10	4.38	4.06</p>
<p>Deficit-GDP ratio with budget cuts	 2.80	 n/a	1.80</p>
<p>Real GDP growth				  2.0	 2.5	 2.7</p>
<p>Inflation					  1.8	 1.5	 1.5</p>
<p>Employment growth				0.5	 0.7	 0.9</p>
<p>Unemployment				    11.7	11.1	10.4</p>
<p>Interest rate on BOT (12-month)	    6.0	 5.7	 5.5</p>
<p>Note - The government says it will make 25 trillion lire of deficit reductions in 1998 to achieve a 2.8 percent deficit-GDP ratio. The document refers to budget deficit reductions of 14.5 trillion lire in 1999 and 6.8 trillion in 2000.</p>
</text>
